What was rewritten: the plugin was a portable manifest pointing an MCP client at
one streamable-HTTP endpoint (https://crosodo.com/api/mcp), with a skill telling
the model to cite the state and county, never to invent statute text, to call
this legal information and not legal advice, and to start a checkout only when
the user clearly asks to buy. This cell is that MCP client in Lisp: the same
endpoint, JSON-RPC over one POST a message (initialize, the initialized
notification, tools/call), the same five unauthenticated tools under the same
names and the same argument members the endpoint declares (state; state and
county; product, state, county, email and idempotencyKey; certId), each also a
verb in the crosodo package, plus /crosodo and a manual topic. The skill's
rules are the cell's primer, and the tool list, which the original read from
the live server every session, is here five tools plus crosodo_call, which
forwards any tool the endpoint grows. What was left out: the two dashboard
tools the endpoint now also lists (get_my_dashboard, log_sale) need an OAuth
sign-in the original never offered, so they are reachable through crosodo_call
but not given a schema of their own; the npm stdio proxy the repository also
publishes (crosodo-mcp) is a second transport to the same server and is not
needed by a cell that speaks the remote one; and no MCP client library is
bundled -- the transport is the image's own HTTP call, so nothing is installed
or fetched at run time.
